All,

Conventional wisdom is that PE is good for rocky sites.

When presented with this opinion in the market you should enquire after why=
 they think this is so.

Whatever the response you should caution that the embedment requirements ar=
e the same for PE and PVC.  Specifically they must both be protected from r=
ocks and that they are both susceptible to rock impingement failures and fa=
ilures due to scraping damage.  These are long term failures.

This can be found on the PPI website and in AWWA Manuals M23 and M55.  Inst=
allation practices for PVC and PE respectively.

The struggle for PE all these decades has been to reduce its vulnerability =
to Slow Crack Growth failures including those induced by rock impingement. =
 The current 4710 compounds are better than previous generations but that h=
as not caused the recommended installation practice to be changed.  Namely =
that PE must be protected from rocks.

The point of this simple tactic besides relating true and valuable informat=
ion is to counter the PE "cures all that ails" mantra.

J



--_000_4414AEBBCFB2B648B49E5766D309768E98037C9D3FMAIL_
